# Implementation Plan - Medicine Availability & Emergency Pharmacy Finder (MediFind)

This document details the architecture, file structure, database design, API specifications, and premium UI mockups for the **MediFind** MERN application.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **API Key & Database Fail-safes:**
> - To make this application work instantly without external accounts, the backend will implement a **dual-database mode**. If no MongoDB connection string is provided in `.env`, the server will automatically fallback to an in-memory or file-based local database (JSON-like local store).
> - For **Cloudinary**, if no credentials are provided, the server will save prescription uploads to a local `uploads/` directory and serve them statically.
> - For **Google Maps**, we will implement a Leaflet.js-based mapping system styled beautifully as the default/fallback view. It requires no API key, works offline/online, and has gorgeous custom markers. If a Google Maps API Key is provided, the frontend can load the Google Maps API.

